    "title": "All 640 Costco warehouses inching closure to mass 24-hour blackout across the US",
    "text": "COSTCO will close all of its warehouses for an entire day in a matter of weeks. The warehouse retailer will close for Easter Sunday this year, which falls on April 5. Sign up for the Money newsletter Thank you! Costco is closing for Easter Sunday on April 5Credit: Getty Costco closes several times throughout the year to recognize national holidays. These include New Year’s Day, Memorial Day, Independence Day, Labor Day, Thanksgiving Day, and Christmas Day. Shoppers are advised to get to their local warehouse before April 5 and stock up on Easter goodies to avoid delays. Although the warehouses will be closed, the Costco website should still be operational. Any online order made on April 5 will likely not be processed until the following day. Costco is joining several other retailers closing for Easter Sunday this April. Retailers closed for Easter Sunday 2026 1. Costco 2. The Container Store 3. Burlington 4. Bob’s Discount Furniture 5. Bloomingdale’s 6. Best Buy 7. Banana Republic 8. Apple 9. True Value 10. T.J. Maxx 11. Staples 12. Sam’s Club 13. Publix 14. Nordstrom 15. Michaels 16. Marshalls 17. Macy’s 18. JCPenney 19. HomeGoods 20. Hobby Lobby 21. Crate & Barrel 22. Ace Hardware 23. Supercuts 24. Target 25. Goodwill 26. Dick’s Sporting Goods 27. Lowe’s Target will close this Easter, alongside Hobby Lobby, Kohl’s, Aldi and Lowe’s, as well as dozens more. This list includes Burlington, Best Buy, Staples, Sam’s Club, JCPenney and Goodwill. Most read in Money Some stores might be open with limited hours, so it’s wise to use the online locator tools. Searching for your address in these tools allows you to see the specific opening hours of stores in your area. Normal operations are expected to continue at all of these stores on Monday, April 6. Costco is joining several other retailers closing for Easter Sunday this AprilCredit: Getty Comments",
